Z||000002||theogre||11-23-2000||04:09 PM||||doesn't matter much. The V6 engines are pretty much all the same. It's all the electrical stuff you need to be carful with. The sensors are the same but there are a couple diferant ECM's. You have to make sure the PROM is correct for the ECM used <I>and</I> for your engine/tranny set.||||reg||1
Z||000003||2M4 Dale||11-24-2000||08:30 PM||||WOW !!!!!!!!!!! I have just bought a "NEW" 1989 Fiero 2.8L V6.......NEW !!!!!! Thanks Jeff , this is the engine that you led me to. <P>Here's the story....These motors were assembled and ready for installation at the Factory when Pontiac stoped production. The engines sat around for a few years and then Pontiac donated them to a local school shop class.....The engines then went into storage at the school and were never touched and are "as new". The fellow That I have bought it from had a connection at the school and when the school cleaned house he ended up with 3 engine assemblys. One of the assemblys is complete with transaxle and cradle......he's keeping that one I guess. The other one is going to Canada and the third one is going to Mansfield....YE HAW<P>So much for my tired old Iron Duke !!! ||||reg||14
Z||000004||Cooter||11-24-2000||08:42 PM||||That is pretty cool! The trade school my dad teaches at has an old/new Citation with a muncie 4 speed. It has 6 miles on it! When they get finished cutting the car up, the tranny is coming with me, then it will get some 4.10's and a new home  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif"><BR>Good find!||||reg||1
